<http://www.spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/event/72001ANHVHCLGLNCCVMNNJLHCJHVKDPJB>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Cat Clyde";
  schema:description """
	Cat Clyde's fourth full-length and first release with Concord Records finds her at a transformative point in her life. Produced by Drew Vandenberg (Faye Webster, S. G. Goodman), Mud Blood Bone meets at a sonic crossroads — the rockabilly grit of Sierra Ferrell melding with the evocative folk rock volatility of Big Thief — as Clyde charts a long journey to reshape the meaning of love in her life. It’s a trudge through the swamp and into vast, cleansing waters that finds Clyde at a critical point of personal evolution—equal parts despair, invocation, discovery, and celebration.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ahead of and throughout her writing sessions for Mud Blood Bone, Clyde looked to her indigenous Métis roots and invoked a deep reverence for nature in efforts to redefine her relationship with love in her life. Learning from the natural world, she took solace in its cyclicality.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The new songs exude nomadic independence: penned in her 1973 Boler trailer on a farm in Ontario, on a narrow boat in England, or in transit from one festival to another, letting lyrics stream freely from a jetlagged dream state. The result is uninhibited, raw, pure; it’s the sound of personal truth discovered in real time.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-09-13T19:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/files/0219cc30-459a-4819-b226-c2acc6aadd08.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/location/401ANPJQJQPQMRSBDNMVNLSPGTRBVQVRH>;
