<http://www.spektrix.com/yukonartscentre/event/72801ATSHJLPCLMCSJGLVNVVHQRQSJNCV>
  a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Jazz on the Wing: Trombonist Audrey Ochoa";
  schema:description """
	“... a musician with endless confidence and skill, navigating varying moods and tempi within an ensemble that is always in sync.” - Critic Keith Black, Winnipeg Free Press <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>2025 Juno Award nominee Audrey Ochoa is a trombonist and composer whose work defies easy categorization.  She plays any of jazz, rock, pop, latin, punk, ska, fusion blends and more. Unbound by rigid ideas of genre or delivery, she pairs meticulous, influential compositions with a playful and liberated approach. Classically trained yet driven by a deep curiosity across styles, Ochoa has built a career rooted in versatility, originality, and craft.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>She has shared the stage with leading Canadian artists including Hilario Durán, PJ Perry, and Tommy Banks, as well as international greats such as members of the Dave Matthews Band, Lew Tabackin, Marcus Miller, Chris Potter, and the UNT One O’Clock Lab Band. A fixture of the Canadian music scene and a rising force internationally, <span><br/></span>Audrey Ochoa – trombone, Chris Andrew – piano, Jeremiah McDade – tenor saxophone, Michael Lent – upright bass, Jon May - drums<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>SPECIAL OFFER UNTIL SEPT 27, BUY 5 Jazz on the Wing tickets FOR THE PRICE OF 4.<span><br/></span>Adults: $132, Youth: $60<span><br/></span>Purchase at Yukon Arts Centre Box Office 667-8574 by phone or in-person.   <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Jazz on the Wing cabaret<span><br/></span>Presented by Jazz Yukon<span><br/></span>More info: jazzyukon.ca<span><br/></span>
""";
