opment and creative exploration.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>The evening will feature Caleb Tomlinson, Local Boy, Kim Beggs, Sweet Jones, and Fraser Canyon & Beyond Hope Band, who will share the fruits of their work, discoveries, and artistic development with the public.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This residency is led by Music Yukon in partnership with Franconnexion.info and Indie Montréal. Together, they bring two cohorts of Yukon artists—Francophone and Anglophone—together for an immersive program focused on “The Lifecycle of an Album & Live Performance Coaching.”<span><br/></span>The Francophone cohort will perform on Saturday, August 29, followed by the Anglophone cohort on Sunday, August 30.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Come discover the unique voices and sounds of Yukon artists and celebrate the culmination of an intensive period of artistic development, collaboration, and creative exchange.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>We look forward to welcoming you!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>
""";
