  schema:name "The Hobbit";
  schema:description """
	The Yukon Arts Centre is thrilled to present The Hobbit, based on the beloved novel by J.R.R. Tolkien and adapted for the stage by Kim Selody. Join Bilbo Baggins as he leaves the comfort of home for an unforgettable journey across Middle-earth alongside a band of determined dwarves and the wizard Gandalf. Along the way, Bilbo encounters trolls, goblins, elves, giant spiders, riddles, dragons, and discovers that true courage can be found in the most unlikely of heroes. Filled with imaginative storytelling, puppetry, music, and theatrical magic, this family-friendly adventure celebrates friendship, bravery, and the power of stepping into the unknown.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Running Time: Approximately 2 hours, including one 20-minute intermission.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Based on the novel by J.R.R. Tolkien<span><br/></span>Stage Adaptation by Kim Selody<span><br/></span>Licensed by Middle-earth Enterprises<span><br/></span>Creative Team<span><br/></span>Director – Katelyn Morishita*<span><br/></span>Producer – Casey Prescott<span><br/></span>Production Manager – Josh Jansen<span><br/></span>Stage Manager – Kennedy Greene*<span><br/></span>Assistant Stage Manager – Gloria Mok<span><br/></span>Lighting Designer – Martin Nishikawa<span><br/></span>Sound Designer/Music Director – Hannah Mazurek<span><br/></span>Costume Designer – Chantal Lefreniere<span><br/></span>Props Designer – Christopher Gwynne Thompson<span><br/></span>Puppet & Dragon Designer – Annie Johnsgaard<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>* Katelyn Morishita and Kennedy Greene appear with the permission of Canadian Actors' Equity Association.<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-10-18T14:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
